 Saturday, October 17!</strong></p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">From experimental avant-garde nightmares to pitch-black comedy and edge-of-your-seat psychological thrillers, the <strong>2026 LHFF 3-Block Pass</strong> guarantees your seat for the entire afternoon short film marathon at a special bundled price.</p><h3 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">\uD83D\uDCFD\uFE0F Included Screening Lineup:</h3><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>12:00 PM \u2014 Block 1: Twisted Visions &amp; Heart-Stopping Horror</strong></p><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><em>Experimental, avant-garde, boundary-pushing horror combined with pure, visceral, traditional horror. Includes post-screening discussion.</em></p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>2:00 PM \u2014 Block 2: Dead Funny</strong></p><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><em>Horror/Halloween comedy, dark humor, and delightfully twisted laughs.</em></p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>3:45 PM \u2014 Block 3: Mind Games</strong></p><ul data-rte-list=\"default\"><li><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><em>Psychological and tension-driven thrillers designed to mess with your head. Includes post-screening discussion.</em></p></li></ul></li></ul></div>\n\n\n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n    \n    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 2px;\n    \n      --tweak-text-block-stroke-color: hsla(var(--black-hsl), 1)\n;\n      \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n\n  }\n\n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 .sqs-html-content {\n    \n    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;\n  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;\n}\n\n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend\n  );\n      border-radius: var(--tweak-text-block-radius);\n  }\n\n  \n  \n#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n      --tweak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px;\n    }\n\n\n  \n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n      --tweak-text-block-blend\n  : normal;\n    }\n  \n\n  #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n    --blur-value: blur(15px);}\n\n</style>\n\n<style id=\"override-container-styles\">\n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n            \n\n#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  \n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 .sqs-html-content {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n        }</style>\n<style class=\"transform-vars\">\n    #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791067778653_3746 {\n      --opacity: 100%;\n      --translate-x: 0px;\n      --translate-y: 0px;\n      --rotation: 0deg;\n      --scale-x: 100%;\n      --scale-y: 100%;\n      --skew-x: 0deg;\n      --skew-y: 0deg;\n      --origin-x: 50%;\n      --origin-y: 50%;\n      --block-transform: none;\n\n      opacity: var(--opacity, 1);\n      transform: var(--block-transform);\n      transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y);\n    }\n  </style><style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n\n\n\n</div>\n</div></div></div></div></div>","excerpt":"<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Mind Games (1:32 hr) + Discussion</p>","location":{"mapZoom":12.0,"mapLat":40.7207559,"mapLng":-74.00076130000002,"markerLat":40.7207559,"markerLng":-74.00076130000002,"addressTitle":"","addressLine1":"","addressLine2":"","addressCountry":""},"customContent":null,"likeCount":0,"commentCount":0,"publicCommentCount":0,"commentState":2,"unsaved":false,"fullUrl":"/now-playing/mind-games-psychological-tension-driven-thrillers","assetUrl":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5ff89563cc0dcd7be5b5a538/1789586834680-EKOGLGZO0CNWYQI5TOBE/3_mind_games.png","contentType":"image/png","structuredContent":{"_type":"CalendarEvent","startDate":1792266300572,"endDate":1792273200572},"startDate":1792266300572,"endDate":1792273200572,"items":[],"pushedServices":{},"pendingPushedServices":{},"originalSize":"7979x5338","recordTypeLabel":"event"},{"id":"6a7d136fd885ff110f6cf42c","collectionId":"61e5f224b5857c262628f32d","recordType":12,"addedOn":1786583127892,"updatedOn":1790529524983,"starred":true,"passthrough":false,"tags":[],"categories":[],"workflowState":1,"publishOn":1786583127892,"authorId":"602eb52c9c36aa5e918c03b5","systemDataId":"1786581904503-VPZ4N8K2RRH3MWP173PJ","systemDataVariants":"1920x1080","systemDataSourceType":"JPG","filename":"Vincent-Price-1920x1080-1 (1).jpg","mediaFocalPoint":{"x":0.5,"y":0.5,"source":3},"colorData":{"topLeftAverage":"000000","topRightAverage":"000000","bottomLeftAverage":"000000","bottomRightAverage":"000000","centerAverage":"000000","suggestedBgColor":"2d2d2d"},"urlId":"vincent-price-what-keeps-us-alive","title":"2026 LHFF Vincent Price: What Keeps Us Alive","sourceUrl":"","body":"<div class=\"sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12\" data-layout-label=\"Post Body\" data-type=\"item\" id=\"item-6a7d136fd885ff110f6cf42c\"><div class=\"row sqs-row\"><div class=\"col sqs-col-12 span-12\"><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.html\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" data-website-component-id=\"3ab239505657d6b5e69c\" id=\"block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\"><div class=\"sqs-text-block-container\">\n  \n  <div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>A NJ Premiere Screening:</strong> The fully authorized Vincent Price documentary reveals far more than the man behind Hollywood\u2019s master of the macabre. It traces a life of elegant contradictions: a classically trained actor who redefined screen villainy with charm and intelligence, an erudite art lover and seasoned gourmand who found equal joy in low-budget horror and high culture, and\u2014ironically, in his later years\u2014a warm, avuncular patriarch to generations who grew up on his films, television appearances, and iconic voice. Through rare archives and deeply personal interviews, the film explores how Price embraced this unexpected cultural role, transforming from a suave antagonist into a beloved mentor figure whose presence felt both timeless and reassuring.</p><p style=\"text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Directed by Matthew Miele, an award-winning documentary filmmaker whose work explores the lives, institutions, and cultural figures that leave a lasting imprint on our collective memory. Through acclaimed films produced and directed through Quixotic Endeavors, he looks beyond public reputation to uncover what a celebrity, artist, writer, filmmaker, or institution reveals about something larger: mortality, legacy, truth, creativity, identity, and endurance. His films are less concerned with biography than with the deeper meaning of a life and what remains after the applause, the reviews, and the headlines. Thank you Matthew, for bringing this film to the LHFF!</p></div>\n\n\n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c {\n    \n    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 6px;\n    \n      \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n\n  }\n\n  #block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c .sqs-html-content {\n    \n    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;\n  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;\n}\n\n  #block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c {\n      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend\n  );\n      border-radius: var(--tweak-text-block-radius);\n  }\n\n  \n  \n#block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c {\n      --tweak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px;\n    }\n\n\n  \n  \n\n  #block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c {\n    }\n\n</style>\n\n<style id=\"override-container-styles\">\n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n            \n\n#block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  \n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-3ab239505657d6b5e69c .sqs-html-content {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n        }</style>\n<style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n\n\n\n</div>\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-button button-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.button/ea4eca2c-24a6-44e3-9a5c-84a0030cdb61_1143/website.components.button.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.button/ea4eca2c-24a6-44e3-9a5c-84a0030cdb61_1143/website.components.button.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.button\" data-sqsp-block=\"button\" data-website-component-id=\"bec220cc9909fe90a7a2\" id=\"block-bec220cc9909fe90a7a2\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n\n\n  \n    \n    \n      \n      \n\n\n\n<div\n  class=\"sqs-block-button-container sqs-button-block-container-system_desktop sqs-block-button-container--right \"\n  data-animation-role=\"button\"\n  data-button-size=\"medium\"\n  data-button-type=\"primary\"\n  \n>\n  <a\n    href=\"https://ci.ovationtix.com/35991/production/1286696\"\n    class=\"sqs-block-button-element--medium sqs-button-element--primary sqs-block-button-element\"\n    data-sqsp-button\n    target=\"_blank\"\n  >\n    BUY TICKETS\n  </a>\n  \n\n\n\n</div>\n\n    \n  \n    \n    \n      \n    \n  \n\n\n<style>\n  #block-bec220cc9909fe90a7a2 {\n    --sqs-block-content-flex: 0;\n  }\n\n  \n  \n    \n      \n      \n    \n      \n      \n        \n      \n    \n  \n</style>\n<style class=\"transform-vars\">\n    #block-bec220cc9909fe90a7a2 {\n      --opacity: 100%;\n      --translate-x: 0px;\n      --translate-y: 0px;\n      --rotation: 0deg;\n      --scale-x: 100%;\n      --scale-y: 100%;\n      --skew-x: 0deg;\n      --skew-y: 0deg;\n      --origin-x: 50%;\n      --origin-y: 50%;\n      --block-transform: none;\n\n      opacity: var(--opacity, 1);\n      transform: var(--block-transform);\n      transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y);\n    }\n  </style><style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n</div></div></div></div></div>","excerpt":"<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>Horror fans, unite! </strong></p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">On October 17, ACME  presents the NJ Premiere of <em>Vincent Price: What Keeps Us Alive</em>. Celebrate the life, voice, and spirit of Hollywood's ultimate gentleman of horror. Grab your tickets before they vanish into the night!</p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Directed by Matthew Miele, an award-winning documentary filmmaker whose work explores the lives, institutions, and cultural figures that leave a lasting imprint on our collective memory. </p>","location":{"mapZoom":12.0,"mapLat":40.7207559,"mapLng":-74.00076130000002,"markerLat":40.7207559,"markerLng":-74.00076130000002,"addressTitle":"","addressLine1":"","addressLine2":"","addressCountry":""},"customContent":null,"likeCount":0,"commentCount":0,"publicCommentCount":0,"commentState":2,"unsaved":false,"fullUrl":"/now-playing/vincent-price-what-keeps-us-alive","assetUrl":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5ff89563cc0dcd7be5b5a538/1786581904503-VPZ4N8K2RRH3MWP173PJ/Vincent-Price-1920x1080-1+%281%29.jpg","contentType":"image/jpeg","structuredContent":{"_type":"CalendarEvent","startDate":1792274400572,"endDate":1792281600572},"startDate":1792274400572,"endDate":1792281600572,"items":[],"pushedServices":{},"pendingPushedServices":{},"originalSize":"1920x1080","recordTypeLabel":"event"},{"id":"6ab94c28015ebd1510f23c1c","collectionId":"61e5f224b5857c262628f32d","recordType":12,"addedOn":1790529355682,"updatedOn":1790529535726,"starred":true,"passthrough":false,"tags":[],"categories":[],"workflowState":1,"publishOn":1790529355682,"authorId":"602eb52c9c36aa5e918c03b5","systemDataId":"1790528638587-EKXLCY4GEQ4VRJ3R0SIL","systemDataVariants":"1926x1044","systemDataSourceType":"JPG","filename":"rev-1.jpg","mediaFocalPoint":{"x":0.756785149255414,"y":0.49051264171178566,"source":3},"colorData":{"topLeftAverage":"91d2e4","topRightAverage":"132453","bottomLeftAverage":"b4722c","bottomRightAverage":"272752","centerAverage":"70778a","suggestedBgColor":"625873"},"urlId":"2026-lhff-spotlight-on-cinema-revenge-with-introduction-by-dylan-mayer","title":"2026 LHFF Spotlight on Cinema: \u201CRevenge\u201D with Introduction by Dylan Mayer","sourceUrl":"","body":"<div class=\"sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12\" data-layout-label=\"Post Body\" data-type=\"item\" id=\"item-6ab94c28015ebd1510f23c1c\"><div class=\"row sqs-row\"><div class=\"col sqs-col-12 span-12\"><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.html\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" data-website-component-id=\"ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab\" id=\"block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\"><div class=\"sqs-text-block-container\">\n  \n  <div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><em>About the film: Before surprising awards season with The Substance (2024), writer/director Coralie Fargeat announced herself in a major way via her debut feature REVENGE (2017) - in which a wealthy (married) man brings his young mistress to an exotic isolated location for a romantic getaway, but things are disrupted by the arrival of the man\u2019s sleazy hunting friends\u2026 what happens from there turns into a white-knuckle, razor-sharp, subversive cat-and-mouse thriller of hypnotic beauty and bloody retribution\u2026</em></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">2017, Rated R, 1h48m<em><br></em></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">To be clear: Revenge is not for the faint of heart, for it is gory - however, it must be stressed that writer/director Coralie Fargeat is not interested at all in some kind of gritty \u201Crealism.\u201D Not. At. All. Instead, Revenge\u2019s cinematic language is&nbsp;sleek, subversive, colorful&nbsp;and&nbsp;confident, enjoying eccentric set pieces and operatic violence (think Quentin Tarantino and Mad Max: Fury Road). Fargeat wears her influences with pride and finds&nbsp;\"poetry in the blood\u201D (her words). Her excitement for cinema is painted -nay, splattered!- across the entirety of this picture. Through bright colors, sound effects, music and pacing (elemental techniques Fargeat uses in full force and control) Revenge plays like a rallying call for genre enthusiasts.</p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">This LHFF event will be hosted by Dylan Mayer and is a part of his Spotlight on [Cinema] series, aiming to bring due attention to a versatile lineup of titles&nbsp;and artists.<br><br>Come join for a pre-show presentation by Dylan Mayer in appreciation of Toronto\u2019s Midnight Madness and Coralie Fargeat\u2019s style/influences - as well as a post-screening hangout. We look forward to seeing you there.</p></div>\n\n\n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab {\n    \n    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 6px;\n    \n      \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n\n  }\n\n  #block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab .sqs-html-content {\n    \n    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;\n  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;\n}\n\n  #block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab {\n      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend\n  );\n      border-radius: var(--tweak-text-block-radius);\n  }\n\n  \n  \n#block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab {\n      --tweak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px;\n    }\n\n\n  \n  \n\n  #block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab {\n    }\n\n</style>\n\n<style id=\"override-container-styles\">\n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n            \n\n#block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  \n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-ffb07dfdc35aa97caeab .sqs-html-content {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n        }</style>\n<style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n\n\n\n</div>\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-button button-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.button/ea4eca2c-24a6-44e3-9a5c-84a0030cdb61_1143/website.components.button.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.button/ea4eca2c-24a6-44e3-9a5c-84a0030cdb61_1143/website.components.button.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.button\" data-sqsp-block=\"button\" data-website-component-id=\"e622bc9b79fccf6c2135\" id=\"block-e622bc9b79fccf6c2135\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n\n\n  \n    \n    \n      \n      \n\n\n\n<div\n  class=\"sqs-block-button-container sqs-button-block-container-system_desktop sqs-block-button-container--right \"\n  data-animation-role=\"button\"\n  data-button-size=\"medium\"\n  data-button-type=\"primary\"\n  \n>\n  <a\n    href=\"https://ci.ovationtix.com/35991/production/1292904\"\n    class=\"sqs-block-button-element--medium sqs-button-element--primary sqs-block-button-element\"\n    data-sqsp-button\n    target=\"_blank\"\n  >\n    BUY TICKETS\n  </a>\n  \n\n\n\n</div>\n\n    \n  \n    \n    \n      \n    \n  \n\n\n<style>\n  #block-e622bc9b79fccf6c2135 {\n    --sqs-block-content-flex: 0;\n  }\n\n  \n  \n    \n      \n      \n    \n      \n      \n        \n      \n    \n  \n</style>\n<style class=\"transform-vars\">\n    #block-e622bc9b79fccf6c2135 {\n      --opacity: 100%;\n      --translate-x: 0px;\n      --translate-y: 0px;\n      --rotation: 0deg;\n      --scale-x: 100%;\n      --scale-y: 100%;\n      --skew-x: 0deg;\n      --skew-y: 0deg;\n      --origin-x: 50%;\n      --origin-y: 50%;\n      --block-transform: none;\n\n      opacity: var(--opacity, 1);\n      transform: var(--block-transform);\n      transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y);\n    }\n  </style><style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n</div></div></div></div></div>","excerpt":"<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">This LHFF event will be hosted by Dylan Mayer and is a part of his Spotlight on [Cinema] series, aiming to bring due attention to a versatile lineup of titles&nbsp;and artists.<br><br>Come join for a pre-show presentation by Dylan Mayer in appreciation of Toronto\u2019s Midnight Madness and Coralie Fargeat\u2019s style/influences - as well as a post-screening hangout.<br><br>We look forward to seeing you there.</p>","location":{"mapZoom":12.0,"mapLat":40.7207559,"mapLng":-74.00076130000002,"markerLat":40.7207559,"markerLng":-74.00076130000002,"addressTitle":"","addressLine1":"","addressLine2":"","addressCountry":""},"customContent":null,"likeCount":0,"commentCount":0,"publicCommentCount":0,"commentState":2,"unsaved":false,"fullUrl":"/now-playing/2026-lhff-spotlight-on-cinema-revenge-with-introduction-by-dylan-mayer","assetUrl":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5ff89563cc0dcd7be5b5a538/1790528638587-EKXLCY4GEQ4VRJ3R0SIL/rev-1.jpg","contentType":"image/jpeg","structuredContent":{"_type":"CalendarEvent","startDate":1792282500572,"endDate":1792289700572},"startDate":1792282500572,"endDate":1792289700572,"items":[],"pushedServices":{},"pendingPushedServices":{},"originalSize":"1926x1044","recordTypeLabel":"event"},{"id":"6acc2d91a354073900b5c0ce","collectionId":"61e5f224b5857c262628f32d","recordType":12,"addedOn":1791766152702,"updatedOn":1791766935234,"starred":true,"passthrough":false,"tags":[],"categories":[],"workflowState":1,"publishOn":1791766152702,"authorId":"602eb52c9c36aa5e918c03b5","systemDataId":"1791766022687-7VNH1BZ6NT4GNKA77I02","systemDataVariants":"205x275","systemDataSourceType":"JPG","filename":"Scream.jpg","mediaFocalPoint":{"x":0.5,"y":0.5,"source":3},"colorData":{"topLeftAverage":"1e1f1a","topRightAverage":"10110c","bottomLeftAverage":"292a25","bottomRightAverage":"090a05","centerAverage":"82837e","suggestedBgColor":"81827e"},"urlId":"scream-1996","title":"2026 LHFF Scream (1996) ","sourceUrl":"","body":"<div class=\"sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12\" data-layout-label=\"Post Body\" data-type=\"item\" id=\"item-6acc2d91a354073900b5c0ce\"><div class=\"row sqs-row\"><div class=\"col sqs-col-12 span-12\"><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.html\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" data-website-component-id=\"0a5a0074282017888f3d\" id=\"block-0a5a0074282017888f3d\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\"><div class=\"sqs-text-block-container\">\n  \n  <div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">One year after her mother\u2019s brutal murder, high school student Sidney Prescott is trying to move on. Then a masked killer starts stalking the quiet town of Woodsboro, armed with a knife, a voice changer, and an encyclopedic knowledge of horror movies. As her classmates fall one by one, Sidney realizes the killer is playing by the rules of the genre, and anyone could be behind the mask.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Wes Craven\u2019s sharp, self-aware slasher revived the horror genre in the \u201990s by turning its clich\u00E9s into a deadly guessing game. Starring Neve Campbell, Courteney Cox, David Arquette, Skeet Ulrich, Rose McGowan, and Drew Barrymore in one of the most famous opening scenes in horror history, <em>Scream</em> is equal parts terrifying, funny, and endlessly rewatchable. Thirty years later, it\u2019s still the perfect Halloween-season scare.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>\uD83D\uDD2A BONUS: Your ticket includes </strong><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #F20A0A;\"><strong>FREE entry to the </strong></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://nightmareinnewhope.com/\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #F20A0A;\"><strong><em>Nightmare in New Hope</em> Horror Prop Gallery in New Hope</strong></span></a><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--custom\" style=\"color: #F20A0A;\"><strong> on Sunday, October 18! ($10 value)</strong></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><strong>Make it a double feature of fear.</strong> After the film, step into the gallery to see the season\u2019s biggest draw up close: <strong>Sidney Prescott\u2019s jacket</strong>. It\u2019s on display only through the end of October, so don\u2019t miss your chance to see this piece of horror history before it disappears.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"><em>Watch the movie. Then come and see the jacket. Just don\u2019t answer the phone.</em></p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Rated R | 1h41m</p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\"></p></div>\n\n\n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-0a5a0074282017888f3d {\n    \n    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 6px;\n    \n      \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n\n  }\n\n  #block-0a5a0074282017888f3d .sqs-html-content {\n    \n    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;\n  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;\n}\n\n  #block